# P13-007: the sample-sharding writer

**Goal.** Add `COPY (…) TO 'out' (FORMAT pfile, shard_samples …)` — a writer that
splits one cohort along the **sample** axis into several filesets that share one
`.pvar` (same variants, same order) and each carry their own `.psam` + `.pgen`,
plus a `concat_dim: "samples"` catalog. This is the write-side mate of P13-008's
`read_pfile(…, combine_samples := 'concatenate')` reader and the P13-005 ATTACH
of a sample-sharded catalog.

**Spec/parent:** P13 arc. Depends on nothing to BUILD (its tests use oracles
that exist on `origin/main` today); its concatenated round-trip test and ATTACH
test are added after P13-008 merges (§7). Writer file: `src/pfile_writer.cpp`.
Collision-free with P13-008 (that branch touches `pfile_reader.cpp` only).

---

## STAR

**Situation.** `plinking_duck` writes PLINK filesets from SQL with
`COPY … (FORMAT pfile)`. It already shards along the **variant** axis
(`shard_by '<col>'`): an ordered COPY rolls one `.pgen`/`.pvar` per contiguous
key value, over **one shared `.psam`** (samples constant across variant-shards),
and emits a `concat_dim: "variants"` catalog. There is **no** way to shard along
the sample axis, so a sample-sharded cohort (same variants, disjoint samples)
can only be built by hand — which is what P13-008's test fixtures do today.

**Task.** Build the symmetric writer: split the sample axis into shards that
share **one `.pvar`** and split the `.psam`/`.pgen`, and emit the
`concat_dim: "samples"` catalog that P13-005 ATTACH and P13-008's reader consume.

**Action.** This doc. It settles the one fork (how the split is specified),
pins the catalog output to P13-008's tested fixture, specifies the N-open-writer
engineering, and builds a test plan on today's oracles.

**Result.** Nothing built yet. Design for review.

