## 10. Risks

- **The N-writer staging/cleanup is the real risk** — a mid-stream failure must
  orphan nothing across N shards. Every error path gets a test.
- **Catalog drift from P13-008.** Mitigated by pinning to the tested fixture
  (§3), not the prose format doc, and verifying first.
- **Contiguity vs. input order.** If the IID groups are not contiguous runs of
  the input sample order, either reject (recommended) or the catalog's global
  ordinals would misdescribe the output. Reject keeps the round-trip exact.
